From: Michael Narine <michael@verita-ai.com>
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 17:17:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Print: initialise m_origin to zero

Print::m_origin (the plate origin, Vec3d) is never initialised. Orca's CLI and GUI
always call set_plate_origin() before slicing, but any other caller reads garbage,
and on a heap that is not fresh the G-code coordinates come out like
X9223372036854775.807.

Value-initialise it to zero at its declaration.

Purpose: Fix an uninitialised member: Print::m_origin yields garbage coordinates (X9223372036854775.807) on a non-fresh heap.
SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
Upstream-Status: to be submitted
Orca-Base: v2.4.2
---
diff --git a/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp b/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
--- a/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
@@ -1189,7 +1189,7 @@
     std::vector<unsigned int> m_slice_used_filaments_first_layer;
 
     //BBS: plate's origin
-    Vec3d   m_origin;
+    Vec3d   m_origin = Vec3d::Zero();
     //BBS: modified_count
     int     m_modified_count {0};
     //BBS
